text:
tara: Heads-up: trying Redwood JS TS SDK in an Expo-managed app (Hermes) and it crashes on startup: `TypeError: crypto.getRandomValues is not a function`. Minimal repro attached.
maria: Hermes doesn't include WebCrypto. In RN we usually add `react-native-get-random-values` + Buffer shim. Did you ensure the shim runs before any imports?
tara: I added `import 'react-native-get-random-values'` at top of App.tsx but stack shows failure inside node_modules/@redwood/sdk/dist/index.mjs during module evaluationit runs before my App code.
lee: Metro and Expo entrypoints can evaluate node_modules earlier. Two quick workarounds: 1) create a small `shim.js` and set it as Expo entryPoint so it runs before the app bundle; 2) have the SDK publish a CJS build and a `react-native` or `main` field that Metro prefers.
maria: Also note RN fetch in Expo/React Native does not expose browser ReadableStream. If the SDK assumes `response.body.getReader()` or uses `pipeTo`, it'll blow up. SDK should detect RN and fallback to `arrayBuffer()`/`text()` and emit non-streamed responses.
tara: That's what I seechat streaming path expects incremental tokens but I only ever get the full payload at the end. We need a runtime fallback.
maria: Quick shim that sometimes helps: 
```
// shim.js
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
import { Buffer } from 'buffer';
global.Buffer = Buffer;
if (!global.crypto) {
  global.crypto = { getRandomValues: require('react-native-get-random-values').getRandomValues };
}
```
then set app.json: `{ "expo": { "entryPoint": "./shim.js" } }`
lee: Packaging notes: add `react-native` entry in package.json exports pointing at a CJS bundle, and include `sourceExts`/`mainFields` tweaks in metro.config.js so RN prefers cjs/main: 
```
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    sourceExts: ['js','json','ts','tsx','cjs'],
    mainFields: ['react-native','main','module']
  }
}
```
maria: Another mobile-specific bug: auth refresh + retry logic can replay POSTs and cause duplicate side-effects on flaky networks. RN fetch isn't abortable and our retry wrapper ends up resending the request. Repro: expired token -> request 401 -> SDK refreshes token and replays, concurrent in-flight requests also replay -> server processes duplicates.
lee: Fix: singleflight token refresh (one refresh promise that others await) + optional dedupe window for retries on mobile. Also expose an env toggle to disable autoretry in RN, e.g., `REDWOOD_SDK_AUTORETRY=false`.
maria: I'll prototype a simple mutex around refresh and add tests that simulate RN behavior (no streams, no abort, delayed responses). Also will widen types: `ReadableStream` -> `ReadableStream | ArrayBuffer | string` for response bodies.
tara: Thanks. I'll try shim + entryPoint change and report back. If it works I'll paste the minimal repro into `examples/expo/`.
ci-bot: Created issue #1310: expo/hermes RN compat: polyfills, cjs entry, streaming fallback, auth singleflight. Assigned to lee.
lee: I'll own packaging + example template. If we land these, SDK should work in Expo Go and dev client (Hermes). PRs welcome.
tara: Great, thanks all.
